 elements. It doesn't matter if the elements are listed differently or if one set has duplicates and the other does not.\n\nTo determine which of the given sets is equivalent to $S,$ we start by listing the elements of $S,$ ignoring any duplicates:\n\n$$\n4,\\,{2,4},\\,2,\\,{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only set equivalent to $S$ is ${2,{2},4,{2,4}}$ since it contains the same elements as $S.$\n\nThe other sets are not equivalent to $S:$\n\n- ${2,4}$ is missing the elements ${2}$ and ${2,4}.$ Note that ${2}\\ne 2.$\n\n- ${2,{2},{4},{2,4}}$ is missing the element $4.$ Note that $4\\ne {4}.$\n\n- ${{2},{2,4}}$ is missing the elements $2$ and $4.$\n\n- ${2,4,{2,4}}$ is missing the element ${2}.$ Note that ${2}\\ne 2.$" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398681 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398682 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398683 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398684 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398685 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1077 "selection" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398681 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1080 #uuid "d5bb647b-4cce-5754-83fc-4c7a4d164719" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398681 1081 "{2,{2},4,{2,4}}" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398681 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398681 1084 #uuid "1f594351-7d69-5b82-ab56-b4db6aaba670" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398682 1081 "{2,4}" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398682 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398682 1084 #uuid "3e5dcf18-a6b9-553b-a871-0bc3c2718b05" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398683 1081 "{{2},{2,4}}" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398683 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398683 1084 #uuid "de1759b9-e64e-5632-a63d-7d4aa37be03e" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398684 1081 "{2,4,{2,4}}" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398684 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398684 1084 #uuid "da14cc2c-21a9-55db-9d59-5d5696de6caa" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398685 1081 "{2,{2},{4},{2,4}}" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398685 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398685 1084 #uuid "b87b006b-5e3d-5087-a977-1843b650269c" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398687 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1069 "q-31633" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1071 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na=⟨5,3⟩,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle has velocity $v=⟨-5,-3⟩$ when $t=2,$ calculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1072 #uuid "359dea7b-c28c-5695-9f78-2decd6212dc8" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1074 "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to compute the velocity of the particle.\n\nTo compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨5,3⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 5\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 3\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5t+{C}_{1},\\,3t+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(2)=⟨-5,-3⟩.$ Substituting $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨5(2)+{C}_{1},\\,3(2)+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨-5,-3⟩ & =⟨10+{C}_{1},\\,6+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=-15$ and ${C}_{2}=-9.$ Therefore, the velocity is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨5t-15,\\,3t-9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the times at which the particle is stationary, we solve for the times at which the velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨5t-15,\\,3t-9⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5t-15 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=3, \\\\ 3t-9 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution that satisfies both equations is $t=3,$ so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398688 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398689 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398690 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398691 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398692 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1077 "selection" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398692 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1080 #uuid "77ccd9ba-8bd4-5cef-a96f-0066b2374cc7" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398688 1081 "t=9" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398688 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398688 1084 #uuid "33850b31-c878-5fea-9b61-e81a78da818e" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398689 1081 "t=5" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398689 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398689 1084 #uuid "1e2f25be-663b-5e68-9722-12735bca3998" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398690 1081 "t=15" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398690 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398690 1084 #uuid "971797e1-7cd0-559f-b79c-db991941d744" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398691 1081 "No stationary points" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398691 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398691 1084 #uuid "4018584b-ff8b-5b49-9e0d-0cd138d9f9ef" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398692 1081 "t=3" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398692 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398692 1084 #uuid "adc48da0-7a45-53ff-8426-6904a74735d6" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398693 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398694 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398693 1069 "q-31634" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398693 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398693 1071 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na=⟨3{t}^{2}-10t,2t-4⟩,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle has velocity $v=⟨-18,-8⟩$ when $t=3,$ calculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398693 1072 #uuid "d1d2200e-dbc1-5e87-951b-4fac16df86f2" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398693 1074 "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to compute the velocity of the particle.\n\nTo compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨3{t}^{2}-10t,2t-4⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int (3{t}^{2}-10t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (2t-4)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}-5{t}^{2}+{C}_{1},\\,{t}^{2}-4t+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(3)=⟨-18,-8⟩.$ Substituting $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =⟨(3)^{3}-5(3)^{2}+{C}_{1},\\,(3)^{2}-4(3)+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨-18,-8⟩ & =⟨-18+{C}_{1},\\,-3+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=0$ and ${C}_{2}=-5.$ Therefore, the velocity is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨{t}^{3}-5{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{2}-4t-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the times at which the particle is stationary, we solve for the times at which the velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}^{3}-5{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{2}-4t-5⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3}-5{t}^{2}={t}^{2}(t-5) & =0\\,⇒\\,t=0,5, \\\\ {t}^{2}-4t-5=(t+1)(t-5) & =0\\,⇒\\,t=-1,5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution that satisfies both equations is $t=5,$ so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398695 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398696 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398697 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398698 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398699 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1077 "selection" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398697 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398694 1080 #uuid "2daecc26-2e53-5776-b8fe-ae2b66da8823" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398695 1081 "t=1" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398695 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398695 1084 #uuid "f466dd59-61f4-547d-a107-450511600e57" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398696 1081 "t=0" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398696 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398696 1084 #uuid "556b0b1a-ef70-52c4-a7d0-96bbcbfcc873" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398697 108