 transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{-t}} & =L{{e}^{3t}}+L{-{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =L{{e}^{3t}}-L{{e}^{-t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+1},\\,s>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{{e}^{3t}}-L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(s+1)-(s-3)}{(s-3)(s+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{s+1-s+3}{(s-3)(s+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (3,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-1,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{f(t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(3,\\infty )\\cap (-1,\\infty )=(3,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>3.$" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398741 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398742 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398743 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398744 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398745 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1077 "selection" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398745 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398740 1080 #uuid "1a417b69-1171-54da-bd75-777eee884877" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398741 1081 "\\frac{2s}{(s-3)(s+1)}" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398741 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398741 1084 #uuid "32566370-0baa-5fb1-b7f3-81b3affe8868" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398742 1081 