\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398787 1072 #uuid "6ce970ec-3f9d-57d6-9307-1253ccd1b689" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398787 1074 "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}=[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-t} & 2t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398789 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398790 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398791 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398792 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398793 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1077 "selection" 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398792 13194139533475 17592186045585 true] [17592186398788 1080 #uuid "f91e0298-1d33-5125-a1ef-22a1c3b27757" 1319413953347